course: dictionary
lesson: 10088
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning is right. Thermal is a good example: it can mean heat, warm clothes, or warm air that rises.
explain: «Storks soar on rising warm air called thermals.» The clues are soar and rising warm air, so a thermal is a current of warm air that lifts birds up. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «"qiūkù" means long johns or thermal leggings.» Here the clue is leggings, which are clothes, so thermal describes something that keeps you warm. Try "warm clothes" in the sentence. It fits, so that is the right meaning.
explain: Thermal can also mean having to do with heat, as in «thermal energy». When a word has several meanings, try each one in the sentence and keep the one that fits best.
fact: Thermal means having to do with heat, as in «thermal energy», which is heat energy.
fact: Thermal can also mean made to keep you warm, like a thermal vest or thermal socks.
fact: A thermal is a rising current of warm air; storks, vultures and gliders use thermals to go up.
fact: Thermals is a plural noun that can mean warm underclothes, such as «long johns» worn in very cold weather.
fact: «Thermal springs» are hot springs, such as those in Rotorua in New Zealand.
exercise: «Storks soar on rising warm air called thermals.» What is a thermal in this sentence? | *A rising current of warm air | A cold lake | A type of bird | A pair of warm socks
exercise: «"qiūkù" means long johns or thermal leggings.» What does thermal mean in this sentence? | A hot spring | Having to do with the sun | A rising current of warm air | *Made to keep you warm
exercise: «Thermal springs» are hot springs, as in Rotorua in New Zealand. What are thermal springs? | Cold rivers | Springs for sitting on | *Hot springs | Swimming pools in the snow
test: «Vultures ride thermals, columns of warm air rising from ground heated by the sun.» What does thermal mean here? | A kind of bird | *A rising column of warm air | Warm underwear | Cold, wet weather
test: Mum says, «Put your thermal vest on, it's freezing.» What does thermal mean in this sentence? | *Made to keep you warm | Having to do with heat energy in science | A hot spring in New Zealand | A rising current of warm air
exam: In «thermal insulators keep heat in», what does thermal mean? | Cold and wet | Made of wool to keep you warm | *Having to do with heat | A rising current of air
